From c1bef771989717e02ac7aabdf90f442cef619696 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:11:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Server] Let StreamableHttpTransport opt out of the
 empty-middleware warning

Framework integrations such as Drupal's mcp_server pass `middleware: []` on
purpose because CORS and trusted-host validation already happen in the
framework's own HTTP layer. Since a transport is created per request, the
warning was logged once per MCP request.

Add a `$warnOnEmptyMiddleware` constructor argument (default `true`) so an
integration can mark the empty list as deliberate, while an accidental empty
list keeps warning. The warning no longer claims protocol version validation
is disabled: handshake-era traffic always runs through handshakeMiddleware().

Fixes #523
